# Damage in the debug VS match on Final Destination: Link (player 1)
# against a CPU Mario who attacks, two stocks each. Link walks over and
# jabs until Mario's damage is said in the opponents' voice, then waits for
# Mario's hits to make his own said in your voice: each figure once it
# holds still, with no label, as the match has one opponent. Nothing is
# said at GO. About 25 seconds.
# Run from Git Bash with the debug match switches, muted, so the voices
# render and log their "plays" lines (run_level.py sets the switches):
#   MELEE_DEBUG_VS=cpu MELEE_DEBUG_VS_STOCKS=2 \
#     python tools/a11y/drive.py --muted tools/a11y/match_damage.drive

# Start on the title screen goes straight into the debug match.
wait "state 0 scene 0$"
press Start until "boot scene: state \d+ scene 2$"
sleep 3

# Link walks over and jabs until Mario's damage settles and is said; nothing
# was said at GO.
press Right 1200
search 'voice opponents: "\d+"$' A*12
wait 'voice opponents plays: "\d+" '

# Mario's attacks: Link's damage, once it holds still.
wait 'voice yours: "\d+"$' 40
wait 'voice yours plays: "\d+" '
sleep 1
